speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I would just like to raise a quick point.
The government House leader and the Whip for our party have both raised a concern about the metal detectors. I must say that I have some concern, which I know is shared by some of my colleagues in this corner of the House, at this matter being raised publicly in this way at this time;
Therefore it seems to me it is important that a decision be made quickly as to what is going to happen in response to it. TTie country now knows of our security arrangements here and the possible loopholes in it. I would urge the government and yourself, Sir, to deal with this matter promptly.
